From d37adb4dfad91823378f7a796be781169c622694 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Lam <matthew.lam@openrouter.ai>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 18:13:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Make pstack tool-neutral

Fixes only, all other pstack wording verbatim:
1. Every model-roles read and write names ~/.config/pstack/models.md, a
   symlink to the tracked plugins/pstack/models.md (Matthew's roles).
2. Codex ignores disable-model-invocation, so every skill gets
   agents/openai.yaml with policy.allow_implicit_invocation: false.
   Explicit $pstack:<skill> still works. poteto-mode and make-bot-ui get
   hyphenated frontmatter names so $pstack:poteto-mode resolves.
3. A role whose model the tool can't select natively runs with
   codex exec -m <slug>, and one marked sentence maps Task /
   subagent_type / readonly to the tool's own subagent tool.
4. Claude Code and Codex transcript paths are named next to the Cursor ones.
5. The repo's verify-* skill / driver is offered next to control-cli and
   control-ui.
6. The repo's review bots (e.g. Bugbot, Devin, perry) are named where pstack
   triages Bugbot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
